config BR2_PACKAGE_INFINITY6E_USBFS
	bool "infinity6e usbfs mmap fix"
	depends on BR2_LINUX_KERNEL
	help
	  Two usbfs fixes for the SigmaStar Infinity6E 4.9.84 kernel,
	  backported from mainline (OpenIPC/linux#280):

	    - usbdev_mmap() maps coherent (uncached) DMA memory to
	      userspace as cached, so libusb zero-copy buffers
	      (libusb_dev_mem_alloc) read stale cache lines;
	    - double free of usb memory on a submiturb error.

	  Remove once OpenIPC/linux#280 is in the kernel tarball.
